# Engineering Rules

1. Inspect the existing repository before creating architecture.
2. Reuse existing auth, API, DB, ORM, components and design tokens.
3. Do not replace working infrastructure without documenting why.
4. Business rules must be enforced server-side.
5. Validate all input at API boundaries.
6. Never trust role/permission information supplied by the client.
7. Keep domain logic out of presentation components when practical.
8. Use typed contracts between frontend and backend where the existing architecture supports them.
9. Never hardcode secrets.
10. `omegon.info@gmail.com` is the development SuperAdmin identity; bootstrap it through safe configuration/seed logic, never a hardcoded password.
11. Preserve data ownership boundaries between Director, Administrative, Teacher and Student.
12. Prefer idempotent migrations/seeds.
13. Add loading, empty, error and success states for real async operations.
14. Never display success unless the backend operation succeeded.
15. Avoid premature abstraction, but keep domain entities extensible.
16. Add tests around authorization and the 15/85 financial rule.
17. Every new route must be reflected in `ROUTE-MAP.md`.
18. Every completed/discovered task must be reflected in `TODO.md`.
19. Every PR must keep roadmap and implementation state synchronized.
20. Run the narrowest useful validation first, then broader checks before merging.
